Target & Compatibility

    Operating environment requires American Truck Simulator (ATS) v1.60+ or v1.61.

    Master file paths encompass /unit/hookup/animated_gate.sii, /unit/hookup/animated_gate.dlc_*.sii, and /unit/hookup/parked_vehicle.sii.

    Cross-compatibility is verified for the ATS Base Map, all official State DLCs, ProMods Canada, and Reforma Map Combos.

Core Parameter Standards

    Universal high-speed approach range is locked at 125.0m for Illinois (dlc_il), New Mexico (dlc_nm), and Texas (dlc_tx) assets.

    Extended trailer clearance range increases to 135.0m on Oregon heavy metal storage doors (metal_01) to eliminate trailer tail-swing clipping.

    Pneumatic and short-range industrial parameters are set to 17.0m across Kansas, Montana, Oklahoma, and Wyoming.

    Guard-check and security zones utilize a 20.0m range for borders, ports, and mines.

    Stop-and-go configurations run at 25.0m for river locks and floodgates, keeping toll booths and scale actions at stock values to protect native functionality.

    Collider geometry requires explicit .pmc physical files for custom assets such as ag_nv_wstg and ag_suncrops.

Fleet & Parking Density Architecture
    
    48 Categories
    
    Namespace de-duplication renames base units in parked_vehicle.sii to prevent fatal runtime collisions with base_vehicle.scs and major map mods.

    Deterministic shift weights enforce strict ratios, utilizing 1.5 for active shifts and 0.0 or reduced values for nocturnal periods.

    Yard trailer positioning under Section 38 specifies a daytime weight of 1.6, a night weight of 0.6, and mandatory rear_align: true tags.

    Performance and VRAM optimization applies low_poly_only: true and always_visible: false on background variants, paired with uset g_lod_factor_parked "1.1".

    Lighting rules enforce forced_flare_low_beam: true across all night-shift profiles.

Group Structure Index

    Groups 1 & 2: Maintain stock engine parameters for toll booths with 25m guarded yard arms.

    Group 3: Covers the Base Map and Western/Mountain expansions using 125.0m standard or 17.0m pneumatic ranges.

    Group 4: Manages directional rotary/swing gates and heavy doors between 125.0m and 135.0m.

    Groups 5 & 6: Handle Midwest (dlc_il, dlc_mo, dlc_ia) and Southern DLC expansions.

    Group 7: Controls special dynamic movers and bridge gates using a 25.0m range, 100° orientation, and /sound/world/gate_iron.soundref.

    Group 8: Governs secure industrial sites, mines, refineries, and ports with a 20.0m range and 90° orientation.

    Group 9: Establishes framework settings for future states including North Dakota, Indiana, and South Dakota.
